`getProfile` now returns 404 when the profile doesn't exist. The full suite passes (2 of 2).

The change is in `api/profile.js`:

```js
export function getProfile(users, id) {
  if (!Object.hasOwn(users, id)) {
    return { status: 404, body: { error: { code: "E_PROFILE_NOT_FOUND" } } };
  }
  return { status: 200, body: users[id] };
}
```

- The error body follows the api-rules shape: `{ error: { code: "E_..." } }`, with an uppercase code starting with `E_`.
- I used `Object.hasOwn` rather than a truthiness check, so ids that match inherited object properties (like `constructor`) also return 404.
- The existing-profile path is unchanged.

The existing test only covers the 200 case, and I only touched `api/`, so I didn't add a test for the 404 path. It would go in `test/profile.test.js`, which is outside my owned paths. Nothing is committed.

